<interrogationes unitas="organum_montatio">

  <interrogatio genus="quomodo">
    <quaestio! (>how do I mount a widget on an insula branch from its manifest?
    <responsum symbolum="organum_legere_genus organum_ramum_parare insula_ramus insula_ramus_radix" via="lib/colloquia_visus.c">Two
      calls: organum_legere_genus(piscina, intern, "genus", praefixum)
      gets the embedded manifest merged with organum_commune, then
      organum_ramum_parare(organum, &amp;ramus, systemata,
      attributa_addita, clavis, piscina, intern) puts the generated
      canon on the branch, creates the starting element, restores saved
      state, installs owners and registers with dimissio.
      lib/colloquia_visus.c mounts on insula_ramus(repo, "colloquia", id)
      or, without an id, on insula_ramus_radix(repo).</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="quid">
    <quaestio! (>what is the difference between organum_legere_genus and organum_legere_viam?
    <responsum symbolum="organum_legere_genus organum_legere_viam organum_infixum_textus" via="lib/organa_infixa.c tools/organa_infigere.sh">organum_legere_genus
      reads the manifest COMPILED INTO the binary (lib/organa_infixa.c,
      generated by tools/organa_infigere.sh from every
      apps/GENUS/organum.stml); apps use it, so an installed binary runs
      from any directory. organum_legere_viam reads a manifest from disk
      (radix + "/" + via) plus radix/apps/organum_commune.stml, for tests
      and tools; with radix NIHIL both paths are relative to the cwd.
      Both return NIHIL on failure and print parse errors or a missing
      (or empty) manifest to stderr with your praefixum ("organum" when
      NIHIL); a NIHIL argument and a base-field collision return NIHIL
      silently.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="cur">
    <quaestio! (>why does my edited apps/X/organum.stml not change the running app?
    <responsum symbolum="organum_legere_genus" via="tools/organa_infigere.sh lib/organa_infixa.c probationes/probatio_organum_montatio.c lib/organum.worklog.md">Apps
      read the embedded copy, never the disk: two sources of truth
      would let an installed binary silently differ from the tree, so
      there is no fallback. Regenerate lib/organa_infixa.c with
      tools/organa_infigere.sh (the fabrica action organa_infixa) and
      rebuild. probatio_organum_montatio (section infixa_fontes) names
      any stale manifest (worklog S7c-1).</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="quomodo">
    <quaestio! (>how do I add my own attributes to the widget's starting element?
    <responsum symbolum="organum_ramum_parare organum_initium" via="lib/admonitiones_visus.c">Pass
      them as attributa_addita, raw STML attribute text that BEGINS
      WITH A SPACE, e.g. " focus=\"admonitiones\"" (lib/admonitiones_visus.c).
      It is pasted unchanged after the manifest defaults
      (organum_initium) in &lt;genus id="..." defaults addita/&gt;, so a
      missing space or an unescaped quote breaks the element and the
      mount fails with "elementum initiale". NIHIL = none. On a child
      branch an element that already exists is left untouched (your
      attributes are not applied); on the root branch only the
      attributes the root lacks are added.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="quid">
    <quaestio! (>what are StatusSystemata and the clavis argument for?
    <responsum symbolum="StatusSystemata organum_ramum_parare conservatio_ramum_addere dimissio_ramum_addere">StatusSystemata
      holds the repository-wide systems: conservatio (saved state),
      relatio, dimissio. A NIHIL field means that system is absent, and
      a NIHIL pointer means none (tests). With conservatio and a
      non-NIHIL clavis, organum_ramum_parare restores the branch's saved
      fields under that key; dimissio registers the branch's popover
      fields. relatio is NOT touched: binding the document stays with the
      widget. For nested mounts pass the branch path as clavis, since
      the same id under different parents would share one saved record.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="possumne">
    <quaestio! (>can a failed organum_ramum_parare leave the branch partly set up?
    <responsum symbolum="organum_ramum_parare insula_ponere_canonem insula_ramus_canonem_ponere insula_ramum_initiare">Yes.
      The canon is set first (on the repository for the root branch,
      otherwise on the branch), then the element is initiated; if
      initiation fails it returns FALSUM with the canon already in
      place. After a successful initiation the restore, owners and
      dimissio steps ignore their own results, so VERUM does not prove
      that state was restored.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="possumne">
    <quaestio! (>can I tell why organum_legere_viam returned NIHIL when the manifest parsed fine?
    <responsum symbolum="organum_legere_viam organum_legere_genus organum_basim_addere">Not
      from stderr: parse errors and a missing file are printed, but when
      organum_basim_addere refuses the merge (a field in your manifest
      has the same name as one in organum_commune) both readers return
      NIHIL and print nothing. Rename the colliding field.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

</interrogationes>
